{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476953382,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgzMDI1MTA3OA=="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1476953934,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NTA0OTAxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1036#issuecomment-255049016"},"message":"Hm. Right, it assumes there is an URL, since this is what is required by `git remote add`. However, this is not true if there's just an entry in `git/config`, that was added without invoking `remote add`. I agree, this is not as reliable as it should be. But I'm not sure what you expect it to behave like. Do you think it should return a remote only if there is an URL and ignore an entry like the one you generated here?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476954123,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NTA0OTczMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1036#issuecomment-255049730"},"message":"I don't know. `git remote` also reports it like this, so we could consider it as \"by design\", but given that some parts of the code mix these two cases together there is at least one bug....somewhere.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1476954901,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NTA1MjcyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1036#issuecomment-255052720"},"message":"Yes, I think we should stick to git's behaviour at this level and consider code making invalid assumptions about `get_remotes` to be the bug.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1508071956,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNjcwOTYxMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1036#issuecomment-336709610"},"message":"Solved for quite some time now. We have an option `with_urls_only`.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1508071956,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI5MzczMjA1Ng=="},"status":2}]}